In article <1993Apr23.203747.945@math.utexas.edu>, nzook@vendela.ma.utexas.edu (Nathan Zook) writes:
>I've seen it mentioned, but at what level is the quest usually?  

I forget exactly.  It varies from game to game.  I think it's usually in 
the 11-15 range.

>BTW, for
>you with itchy fingers, I make it a POINT not to decend too quickly. I tend
>to stay on a level until the monsters have pettered out, I'm out of food, AND
>just prayed.  Not rare to hit 2nd level of dungeon AFTER 5th level player.
>Of course, wizards tend to be a little cautious.
>
Sounds like a little too slow to me.  I typically find my experience
level is equal to the dungeon level for the first few levels.  Remember
that the monsters which appear are (generally) proportional to your level,
not the dungeon level.  So if you go through a level teleport trap to 
level 10 when you're at Exp level 1, you don't need to worry all that much...

When I start, I figure I need to find something useful soon (the usual 
list: speed boots, a good weapon, a bunch of good scrolls/wands/potions, 
...).  The best place to find a whole bunch of stuff is a shop.  Since 
there are never any shops on level 1, I usually leave level 1 as soon as 
possible.

The only reason I hang around any level for a long time is if I find an
altar and I want to sacrifice a lot (to get a weapon, fix my prayer 
timeout, etc.).  I guess I also might hang around a shop level for a
while if I want something out of it and can't pay (fetch rover...).

